## Finding P

Write $P = B + t(M - B) = \left(13 - \tfrac{31t}{4},\, 3t\right)$ on segment $BM$. The condition $\angle APC = 90°$ gives $(A-P)\cdot(C-P) = 0$:
$$\left(-13+\tfrac{31t}{4}\right)\!\left(-\tfrac{70}{13}+\tfrac{31t}{4}\right) + (-3t)\!\left(\tfrac{168}{13}-3t\right) = 0.$$
Expanding and simplifying (multiply through by 208, divide by 5):
$$2873\,t^2 - 7540\,t + 2912 = 0, \qquad t = \frac{7540 \pm 4836}{5748}.$$
The root on $[0,1]$ is $t = \frac{2704}{5748} = \frac{8}{17}$, giving
$$P = \left(\tfrac{159}{17},\, \tfrac{24}{17}\right).$$

**Verification:** $(A-P)\cdot(C-P) = \tfrac{(-159)(-384)+(-24)(2544)}{17\cdot 221} = \tfrac{61056 - 61056}{3763} = 0.$ ✓

## Finding Q

Write $Q = C + s(M - C) = \left(\tfrac{99}{13} - \tfrac{123s}{52},\, \tfrac{168}{13} - \tfrac{129s}{13}\right)$ on segment $CM$. The condition $\angle AQB = 90°$ gives $(A-Q)\cdot(B-Q) = 0$, which expands (over common denominator 2704) to:
$$281385\,s^2 - 707772\,s + 340704 = 0 \;\;\Longrightarrow\;\; 93795\,s^2 - 235924\,s + 113568 = 0.$$
The discriminant is $114244^2$, and the root on $[0,1]$ is $s = \frac{121680}{187590} = \frac{24}{37}$, giving
