with center $O = \left(\tfrac{129}{16},\, \tfrac{267}{64}\right)$.

**Q lies on this circle:** Substituting $Q = \left(\tfrac{225}{37}, \tfrac{240}{37}\right)$:
$$\tfrac{108225}{1369} - \tfrac{29025}{296} - \tfrac{64080}{1184} + \tfrac{585}{8} = \tfrac{2925}{37} - \tfrac{29025}{296} - \tfrac{8010}{148} + \tfrac{585}{8}.$$
Converting to denominator 296: $\tfrac{23400 - 29025 - 16020 + 21645}{296} = \tfrac{0}{296} = 0.$ ✓

